{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Living the Dream", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "A Big Oops!", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Future Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are four different tenses that talk about the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Will: </span><ul><li>When you talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future.</li></ul>For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">I will call you later</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Be going to: </span><ul><li>When you ask about intentions.</li></ul> For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">Are you going to go to the meeting later?</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous: </span><ul><li> When you talk about things that are arranged, on the  agenda or booked for the future.</li></ul> For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">The meeting is happening at 9 a.m. sharp tomorrow. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Simple Present: </span><ul><li>When you talk about schedules. </li></ul>For example: <br><span class=\"italic\"> The presentation starts at 3:30.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I am running errands today.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It's on tonight at five.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I am going to work really hard. I promise.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I will definitely be better than this woman.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking Hypothetically About the Past", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Would have</span>, <span class=\"strong\">should have</span> and <span class=\"strong\">could have </span>can be used to talk about hypothetical situations in the past that may or may not be true.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">Could have</span> (+ past participle)</span></br><span class=\"strong\">Could have</span> expresses an action that was possible at some time in the past, but it wasn't done.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">could have gotten that job</span>, if I applied earlier.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You also use <span class=\"strong\">could have</span> to suggest how an action in the past that was not done would have led to a different situation in the present. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Why is Mark not here yet?</span></br><span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">could have been</span> stuck in traffic or he <span class=\"strong\">could have overslept</span></span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">Should have </span>(+ past participle)</span></br> <span class=\"strong\">Should have</span> is used for giving advice for past events. We often use it to display regret when we think something was a good idea in the past, but we didn't do it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">should have applied</span> sooner</span>. <br/>(I regret not applying sooner).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">shouldn't have answered</span> that question like that.</span></br> (You should have answered that question in another way).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">Would have </span>( + past participle)</span></br>  <span class=\"strong\">Would have</span> expresses a regret about an action you did not do in the past but you now wish you had.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">would have gone </span> to your concert, but I didn't know the date. </span><br/>(I wanted to go to your concert but I didn't know the date, so I didn't go.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "She shouldn't have said that, it comes off as being informal.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She should have answered more formally. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She could have said, \u201cFine thank you. And you?\u201d ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I would have been perfect for this job.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I wouldn't have said that.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to ramble on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to talk without stopping", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  The interviewer is trying to make small talk and she's just rambling on.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear when listening to an interview.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to start off on the wrong foot", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to begin in an awkward or unpleasant way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  This interview has started off on the wrong foot. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "formally", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in a formal way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  She should have answered more formally. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "professionalism", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an attitude appropriate for the workplace", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She should have answered in a way that demonstrated her professionalism. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "positively", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in a good way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Her answer reflected positively on her overall character. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write about a job interview.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain what I regretted.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain what I would have changed.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I reflect on my experience and talk about what I will do next time.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present my story clearly and concisely.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a story about your worst job interview experience.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you don't have one, make one up.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Be very detailed in your description.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What would you have done differently and what you will do next time?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use passive modals to explain what you would have changed.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Get into groups and compare stories.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Vote on the best one.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": tr